{"data": {"intent_id": "fix-69-status-resolver", "text": "Bug fix per GitHub issue #69 in this git worktree: PYTHONPATH=src python3 -m orc_werk.cli status <journal-dir>/<run>/journal.jsonl fails with a misleading ERR-VALIDATION ('fact belongs to a different delivery_run_id', expected 'journal') because _resolve_journal in src/orc_werk/cli/journal_reading.py derives the run id from the filename stem. Fix: in _resolve_journal, when the target is an existing file named exactly journal.jsonl, treat its PARENT DIRECTORY name as the run id and the grandparent as the journal directory (the issue-#55 per-run layout). Keep every existing resolution form working: bare run id, run directory path, legacy <run>.jsonl file. Add unit tests in tests/scenarios/test_cli_housekeeping_55.py (match existing style): status on <dir>/<run>/journal.jsonl succeeds; history on the same path succeeds; a legacy file literally named journal.jsonl inside a flat journal dir (no per-run structure) - choose sensible behavior and assert it. Run bash scripts/check.sh and ensure exit 0. Then git add the changed files and git commit -m 'fix(cli): resolve <run>/journal.jsonl paths per run-dir layout (#69)'. Do not push. Touch only src/orc_werk/cli/journal_reading.py and tests/scenarios/test_cli_housekeeping_55.py."}, "delivery_run_id": "fix-69-status-resolver", "extensions": {}, "id": "FACT-INTENT-SUBMITTED", "kind": "fact", "schema_version": 1, "seq": 1}
